The functor $\mathrm{Ring}^{\mathrm{nu,h}} \to \mathrm{Sp}$ given by $I \mapsto \mathrm{THH}( \mathbb{Z} \ltimes I)$ is
projectively pseudocoherent.

\label{linalg} 
Let $\left\{u_1, \dots, u_n, v_1, \dots, v_n\right\}$ be linearly independent in
$V$. Then the form $\sum_{i=1}^n u_i \wedge v_i$ has weight $n$.

\label{lemma_drw1}
Let $R$ be an $\mathbb F_p$-algebra which is henselian along an ideal $I\subseteq R$. Then
$R-F:W_r\Omega^n_{(R,I)}\to W_{r-1}\Omega^n_{(R,I)}$ is surjective.

\label{finiteetale}
Let $R$ be an $\mathbb{F}_p$-algebra. Then the mod $p$ \'etale cohomological
dimension of $R$ is $\leq 1$.

